# Does it learn by itself? A fresh robot (no experience). A visitor sits in front of it; eight times
# they talk to it and then pet it (voice -> touch, 3 s later). Then four times they only talk.
# The robot should have learned that a voice comes before petting: the link appears in the log
# ("learn: voice -> petting"), and while the visitor only talks it expects petting (expect_reward)
# and asks for it (an eager call, a happy face).
duration 8:00
clock 14:00
seed 21
room_light on
owner home
at 0:05 person v enter 0 1.2
every 0:40 from 0:30 until 5:10 talk 0 2.5 0.8
every 0:40 from 0:33.5 until 5:14 touch_head 500
at 5:50 talk 0 2.5 0.8
at 6:20 talk 0 2.5 0.8
at 6:50 talk 0 2.5 0.8
at 7:20 talk 0 2.5 0.8
